    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-055 — CSS `background:` shorthand (color forms).** One commit. **Docs follow after merge.**\n\nCorrects ADR-054's imprecise finding. A 4-row isolation fixture proved that `border:` shorthand **already works** (ADR-040 shipped `try_expand_border`); only `background:` was failing. ADR-054's fixture changed everything at once, making both look broken.\n\n## What shipped\n\n### `stylesheet.cpp`\n\nNew `try_expand_background` (~25 lines) + dispatcher hook.\n\n**Design decisions:**\n\n- **Color-only v1.** URL forms need `background-image` + `-repeat` + `-position` + `-size` coordination — separate ADR, comparable to ADR-040's border work.\n- **Drop url / gradient / multi-layer entirely** — extracting only the color from `#fff url(x)` produces a *worse* state than dropping (fill but no image, vs. today: neither).\n- **`none` → `transparent`** — CSS spec equivalent.\n- **Raw color string pass-through** — matches `border-color`; layout's `parse_color` resolves at layout time.\n\n### Tests\n\n7 new tests covering: color forms, `none`, `!important`, and three drop cases (`url()`, `gradient()`, multi-layer).\n\n### Fixture\n\n`docs/adr055-background-shorthand-test.html` — 5-row permanent fixture. Tests longhand / shorthand / mixed / cascade order.\n\n## Verified delta (screenshot 2026-11-01)\n\n```\nRow 1 GREEN   -- longhand bg + longhand border (control)\nRow 2 BLUE    -- bg shorthand works (was WHITE pre-ADR-055)\nRow 3 ORANGE  -- border shorthand works (ADR-040, unchanged)\nRow 4 PURPLE  -- both shorthands together\nRow 5 NO FILL -- 'none' correctly overrides #c0392b (was red pre-ADR-055)\n```\n\nAll five rows correct. The synthetic-fixture verification category now has **two consecutive ADR proofs** (ADR-054 rotate, ADR-055 background).\n\n## Wikipedia impact\n\n**7 of 11 `background:` forms now render** — `#fff`, `#ffffff`, `#fff !important`, `var(--x, #fff)`, `none`, `none !important` — the most common article chrome backgrounds.\n\n**4 of 11 still drop entirely** — 3 url() forms + 1 linear-gradient. No regression: same as today (transparent fill, no image, no gradient).\n\n## The ADR-054 correction\n\nThe original ADR-054 claim — \"shorthand background: and border: don't parse yet\" — was imprecise. Actual finding: **only `background:` fails.** Border shorthand was rendered but invisible at 2px against white page.\n\n## Test count\n\n- 651 → 658 cases (+7 new)\n- 2490 → 2514 assertions (+24 new)\n- Zero pre-existing tests affected\n\n## Deferred\n\n- url() forms (3 in Wikipedia CSS)\n- linear-gradient (1 in Wikipedia CSS)\n- Multi-layer (`url(a), url(b)`)\n- `#fff url(...)` compound (part of url forms work)\n\nRefs #246\n",
